  "function": "value_creation_rollup",
  "note": "The roll-up of the value creation views over position rows as they travel (decimal strings, signed dated flows), by hand, as of 2023-06-30. Five positions: P1 and P2 held, P3 realized, P4 held with no bridge (no entry snapshot) and a fee beside its contribution, P5 held with no Locked valuation (no NAV, so no gain). Portfolio, over the three positions whose gain is split (P1, P2, P3): invested 1,000,000 + 1,000,000 + 500,000 = 2,500,000; NAV 1,300,000 + 920,000 + 0 = 2,220,000; distributions 0 + 200,000 + 720,000 = 920,000; value now 3,140,000; gain 300,000 + 120,000 + 220,000 = 640,000 = 3,140,000 - 2,500,000; EBITDA growth 200,000 + 150,000 + 100,000 = 450,000; multiple expansion 50,000 - 90,000 + 60,000 = 20,000; debt paydown 30,000 + 10,000 + 40,000 = 80,000; other 20,000 + 50,000 + 20,000 = 90,000; 450,000 + 20,000 + 80,000 + 90,000 = 640,000. P2 carries no revenue split, so the revenue and margin parts are not a total (never a partial sum). P4 and P5 are counted by reason. Cohorts by entry multiple (edges 10 and 12). Under 10.0x holds P1 and P2: invested 2,000,000, distributions 200,000, NAV 2,220,000, DPI 0.1, RVPI 1.11, MOIC (200,000 + 2,220,000) / 2,000,000 = 1.21; pooled flows -2,000,000 on 2021-06-30 and 200,000 + 2,220,000 on 2023-06-30, 730 days later, so (1 + r)^2 = 1.21 and the IRR is 0.1; EBITDA growth weighted by invested capital (1,000,000 x 0.25 + 1,000,000 x 0.1) / 2,000,000 = 0.175. 10.0x to 12.0x holds P3: -500,000 on 2020-06-30 and 720,000 on 2022-06-30 (730 days), MOIC 1.44, (1 + r)^2 = 1.44, IRR 0.2; a realized position holds no NAV, so no terminal flow. 12.0x and over holds P5: invested 600,000, DPI 0, and no NAV, MOIC or IRR while it has no Locked valuation (no_valuation). Not calculable holds P4: MOIC 880,000 / 800,000 = 1.1 (a fee is not invested capital), and the IRR counts the fee as an outflow: -808,000 on 2022-06-30 and 880,000 on 2023-06-30, 365 days, so r = 880,000 / 808,000 - 1 = 9 / 101 = 0.0891089109. Cohorts by entry net leverage (edge 4): Under 4.0x holds P1 and P2 (as above); 4.0x and over holds P3 and P5: invested 1,100,000, distributions 720,000, DPI 72 / 110 = 0.6545454545, no NAV (P5), EBITDA growth (500,000 x 0.4 + 600,000 x 0.05) / 1,100,000 = 23 / 110 = 0.2090909091. Case 2 is a filter that leaves P1 and P3: invested 1,500,000, NAV 1,300,000, distributions 720,000, gain 520,000 = 300,000 + 110,000 + 70,000 + 40,000, revenue 120,000 + 70,000 = 190,000 and margin 80,000 + 30,000 = 110,000 (both carry the split); P1 alone has (1 + r)^2 = 1.3, IRR sqrt(1.3) - 1 = 0.1401754251; the bands the filter empties keep their rows with a count of 0 and no figure. Case 3 is a filter that leaves nothing: no figure anywhere, never a zero.",
